Data the application downloads or queries (not part of this repository)

- IP geolocation: DB-IP.com Lite databases (IP to City Lite, IP to ASN Lite), CC BY 4.0, "IP
  geolocation by DB-IP.com", https://db-ip.com. They are installed on request by
  `flask datasets update`; the attribution is shown in the footer, on the IP location page, in the
  report and in the JSON export, and must stay wherever the data is shown.
- Public breaches: Have I Been Pwned, https://haveibeenpwned.com, CC BY 4.0.
- Known exploited vulnerabilities: the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog of CISA,
  https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog, which CISA publishes for
  anyone to use. Installed on request by `flask datasets update`.
- Exploit prediction scores: the Exploit Prediction Scoring System (EPSS), FIRST.Org, Inc.,
  https://www.first.org/epss/. FIRST publishes the scores for free (a CSV download and an API,
  no registration) and asks to be named when they are used; the application names EPSS and FIRST
  wherever it shows a score, in the report's list of sources and in the JSON export. Installed on
  request by `flask datasets update`.
- Everything else is queried, not redistributed. Its terms are listed in docs/checks-catalog.md
  (sections 3 and 5); the Shodan InternetDB, for one, is free for non-commercial use only.

Python dependencies are installed from PyPI under their own licences (permissive ones, MPL-2.0 for
certifi and publicsuffixlist, LGPL-3.0 for psycopg, used as an unmodified library); uv.lock lists
the exact set.
